#: components/dashboard/report/chartDocs.ts:33
msgid "Corpus. The publications shown come from OpenAlex, harvested and consolidated by the druid-biblio warehouse of Nantes Université: for each structure, the ETL collects the affiliated publications (ROR identifier / OpenAlex institution of the structure), enriches them (Scimago and Nantilus reference data, signature charter, staff lists) and freezes a snapshot. The figures in the report reflect the state of the data at the date of the last export, not real time."
msgstr "Corpus. The publications shown come from OpenAlex, harvested and consolidated by the druid-biblio warehouse of Nantes Université: for each structure, the ETL collects the affiliated publications (ROR identifier / OpenAlex institution of the structure), enriches them (Scimago and Nantilus reference data, signature charter, staff lists) and freezes a snapshot. The figures in the report reflect the state of the data at the date of the last export, not real time."

#: components/dashboard/report/chartDocs.ts:34
msgid "Scopes. “Affiliation” keeps every publication signed by the structure as disambiguated by OpenAlex. “Staff” restricts to publications where at least one author is matched (by name) to the structure's validated member list: this scope is closer to the actual staff but may leave out publications whose authors are not yet matched. The period filters on publication year; publications without a year are excluded from all charts."
msgstr "Scopes. “Affiliation” keeps every publication signed by the structure as disambiguated by OpenAlex. “Staff” restricts to publications where at least one author is matched (by name) to the structure's validated member list: this scope is closer to the actual staff but may leave out publications whose authors are not yet matched. The period filters on publication year; publications without a year are excluded from all charts."

#: components/dashboard/report/chartDocs.ts:35
msgid "Citation indicators. Citations are OpenAlex counts at the export date. The FWCI (Field-Weighted Citation Impact) compares a publication's citations with the world average of comparable publications (same field, same year, same type): 1 = world average. The “Top 1% / Top 10%” indicators flag publications whose citation count places them in the upper percentiles of their field and year. These indicators are of little significance for recent publications (short citation window) and for small samples."
msgstr "Citation indicators. Citations are OpenAlex counts at the export date. The FWCI (Field-Weighted Citation Impact) compares a publication's citations with the world average of comparable publications (same field, same year, same type): 1 = world average. The “Top 1% / Top 10%” indicators flag publications whose citation count places them in the upper percentiles of their field and year. These indicators are of little significance for recent publications (short citation window) and for small samples."

#: components/dashboard/report/chartDocs.ts:36
msgid "Classifications. Topics, subfields and domains are assigned automatically by OpenAlex from the content of the publications. Journal quartiles come from the Scimago reference (SJR). The open-access status is Unpaywall's, via OpenAlex (diamond, gold, green, hybrid, bronze, closed). Collaborations are inferred from co-author affiliations; OpenAlex institution disambiguation still contains residual errors (homonymous institutions, incomplete affiliations)."
msgstr "Classifications. Topics, subfields and domains are assigned automatically by OpenAlex from the content of the publications. Journal quartiles come from the Scimago reference (SJR). The open-access status is Unpaywall's, via OpenAlex (diamond, gold, green, hybrid, bronze, closed). Collaborations are inferred from co-author affiliations; OpenAlex institution disambiguation still contains residual errors (homonymous institutions, incomplete affiliations)."

#: components/dashboard/report/chartDocs.ts:37
msgid "General limitations. OpenAlex coverage is uneven across disciplines: the humanities and social sciences, publications in French and books are under-represented compared with indexed international journals. Comparisons between structures from different disciplines should therefore be avoided; trends over time within the same structure are more robust. The most recent year is usually incomplete (indexing delays)."
msgstr "General limitations. OpenAlex coverage is uneven across disciplines: the humanities and social sciences, publications in French and books are under-represented compared with indexed international journals. Comparisons between structures from different disciplines should therefore be avoided; trends over time within the same structure are more robust. The most recent year is usually incomplete (indexing delays)."

